/target
/renders

# Presets are user data. The root of `presets/` is whatever the player saved
# and never ships; a *bank* is a folder, and a bank ships whole.
#
# One negation per bank, not per preset (2026-08-06). The old form named all
# 32 shipped presets individually and had already grown past the point of
# being read — `init.json` sat un-negated for a release because nobody
# noticed a missing line in a list that long. A folder is one line, and the
# folder name is the bank's name everywhere: on disk, on its chip in the
# presets pane, and as the credit when the bank is somebody else's.
#
# Adding a contributor's bank is therefore: drop in `presets/<their name>/`,
# add one line here on purpose. That "on purpose" is the whole discipline —
# nothing enters history by being in the right folder alone.
/crates/fibonacci-gui/presets/*
!/crates/fibonacci-gui/presets/BYPO/

# Unconfirmed assets never enter history.
#
# A file in a commit is a file in every clone forever — that is the whole lesson of
# assets/font.otf, which cost a full history rewrite and a reborn repo on
# 2026-08-05 (README: "The Xilla history rewrite — DONE"). These are derivatives of
# source images whose licence is not established, so they stay local until their
# provenance is settled. Ignored rather than merely un-added, because "never run
# git add -A in this repo" is not a rule anyone can keep.
#
# The briefs beside them are ours and stay tracked.
/crates/fibonacci-gui/assets/portraits/*.txt
/crates/fibonacci-gui/assets/*.jpg
/crates/fibonacci-gui/assets/*.png
/docs/
dist/

# Machine-local build acceleration (linker choice). The committed form broke
# every machine but one; each machine keeps its own untracked copy.
/.cargo/config.toml
